          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A conjectural characterization of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+powers"} symmetric powers
            in symmetric monoidal
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℚ
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Q}^{+}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+category"} linear categories
            is given on this page. The description in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+properties"} universal properties
            would be equivalent to a much longer one but much more constructive in algebraic terms. It would be similar to the characterization of products known as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fox+theorem"} Fox theorem
            but where
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/products"} products
            are replaced by
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+powers"} symmetric powers
            = succeed "-algebra." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℚ
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Q}^{+}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CMon-enriched+symmetric+monoidal+categories"} CMon-enriched symmetric monoidal categories
            would involve symmetric and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/divided+powers"} divided powers
            which are equal in this simpler setting. This conjecture seems to be true and if it is really the case, the proof is not trivial.
          %h2#conjecture Conjecture
          %p We suppose that the symmetric monoidal categories are strict monoidal categories.
          %p
